reasoning_content:
Now the new Feature test file, using the Situation kit, proving the cooling spans the six hours the invariant counts (target side and origin side) and stops after it.

Name: `tests/Feature/DispatchRefusalCoolingTest.php`. Function names must be unique globally — I'll use none (Pest `test()` closures don't declare global functions). Good, no function declarations.

Test file content:

```php
<?php

use Modules\AI\Enums\AiWorkKind;
use Modules\AI\Tests\Support\Situation;
use OGame\Models\DebrisField;
use OGame\Models\FleetMission;
use Tests\IsolatedAccountTestCase;

require_once __DIR__ . '/../Support/Situation.php';

uses(IsolatedAccountTestCase::class);

// DISPATCH_REFUSALS: the invariant counts a repeat of the same account + target (or origin) + reason
// inside six hours, so a cooling shorter than that span lets the same refusal be made again inside the
// window it measures (measured 4 Oct 2026: one target refused 21 times in six hours). The harvest beside
// the planet is the story: an ordinary session sends the recyclers, and only the refusal the gate made
// hours ago stops it.

test('a field the gate refused four hours ago is still not the harvest this session sends', function (): void {
    DebrisField::query()->delete();
    FleetMission::query()->delete();

    $home = $this->planetService->getPlanetCoordinates();

    Situation::of($this)
        ->resources(1_000_000, 1_000_000, 1_000_000)
        ->ships('recycler', 2)
        ->debris(40_000, 20_000)
        ->refusedDispatch(galaxy: (int) $home->galaxy, system: (int) $home->system, position: (int) $home->position, reason: 'source_short_at_dispatch', minutesAgo: 240)
        ->session()
        ->expectNoWork(AiWorkKind::Recycle);
});

test('a body the gate refused four hours ago is not the origin this session flies from', ...);

test('the cooling ends and the same harvest flies again', ... minutesAgo: 420 → expectWork(Recycle));
```

Hmm, one concern for the third test: the session might create Recycle work but the field... it's the same story as the passing 'ordinary session recycles' test, so fine.

Also: after `session()` the clock advances to due times; the 420-min-old refusal stays outside. ✔

Another concern: `Situation::of($this)` calls `awake()` which travels the clock. In the *first* test the planted refusal is 240 min before that travelled clock. Fine.

Hmm, but careful: `session()` runs the session planner, which might schedule the Recycle intent at "now" (due now) and then execute it; with the cooling the Recycle candidate is refused at planning, so nothing. ✔

For `expectNoWork(AiWorkKind::Recycle)`: `work()` excludes RunSession; so if the session created no Recycle work → pass.

But careful: could the session create a Recycle work for a *different* debris field left over? We delete fields first. ✔

I'll write the file.

